# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction {#introduction}"
msgstr "Panimula {#introduction}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a chemist runs an NMR experiment, they place a sample of nuclear spins in a strong magnetic field, apply a radio-frequency (RF) pulse, and measure the signal that comes back. The technique rests on a few ideas from the quantum mechanics of a spin-1/2 particle in a magnetic field. The spin has two energy levels separated by an energy that corresponds to a characteristic Larmor frequency. A resonant pulse at that frequency tips the spin into the transverse plane, where it precesses and induces a signal that then fades with two characteristic times, $T_1$ and $T_2$.\n"
msgstr "Kapag nagpapatakbo ng NMR experiment ang isang chemist, naglalagay sila ng sample ng mga nuclear spin sa malakas na magnetic field, naglalapat ng radio-frequency (RF) pulse, at sinusukat ang signal na bumabalik. Nakasalalay ang teknik na ito sa ilang ideya mula sa quantum mechanics ng isang spin-1/2 na particle sa magnetic field. May dalawang antas ng enerhiya ang spin na pinaghihiwalay ng enerhiyang tumutugma sa isang katangi-tanging Larmor frequency. Ang resonant na pulse sa frequency na iyon ay itinutumba ang spin papunta sa transverse plane, kung saan ito nagpe-precess at nag-i-induce ng signal na unti-unting nawawala sa dalawang katangi-tanging oras, $T_1$ at $T_2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A superconducting **qubit** is an engineered version of the same object: a controllable two-level quantum system. Its $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ states are the analog of spin-up and spin-down, the gate we apply to rotate it is the analog of the RF pulse, and it loses coherence with its own $T_1$ and $T_2$. This is not merely a loose comparison; some of the earliest experimental quantum processors in the late 1990s and early 2000s used NMR.\n"
msgstr "Ang superconducting **qubit** ay isang ginawang bersyon ng parehong bagay: isang kontroladong two-level na quantum system. Ang mga estado nitong $|0\\rangle$ at $|1\\rangle$ ay katumbas ng spin-up at spin-down, ang gate na ginagamit natin para i-rotate ito ay katumbas ng RF pulse, at nawawalan ito ng coherence sa sarili nitong $T_1$ at $T_2$. Hindi lang ito basta paghahambing; ilan sa mga pinakaunang eksperimental na quantum processor noong huling bahagi ng 1990s at unang bahagi ng 2000s ay gumamit ng NMR.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this module you will use a real quantum computer to run the same characterization experiments that an NMR spectroscopist (or a quantum engineer calibrating hardware) performs:\n"
msgstr "Sa module na ito, gagamit ka ng totoong quantum computer para patakbuhin ang parehong mga characterization experiment na ginagawa ng isang NMR spectroscopist (o quantum engineer na nagka-calibrate ng hardware):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Rabi / nutation** — driving the spin and watching it rotate. This is how you calibrate a $\\pi$ or $\\pi/2$ rotation.\n"
msgstr "**Rabi / nutation** — pagpapagalaw sa spin at pagmamasid sa pag-ikot nito. Ganito mo ka-calibrate ang $\\pi$ o $\\pi/2$ na rotation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_1$** — spin-lattice relaxation, the decay of an excited spin back to equilibrium.\n"
msgstr "**$T_1$** — spin-lattice relaxation, ang pagbalik ng excited na spin sa equilibrium.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_2$** — spin-spin relaxation (dephasing), measured with a Ramsey experiment and refocused with a Hahn echo.\n"
msgstr "**$T_2$** — spin-spin relaxation (dephasing), sinusukat gamit ang Ramsey experiment at nire-refocus gamit ang Hahn echo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**NMR spectroscopy (chemical shift and $J$-coupling)** — simulating a small molecule on several qubits and reading its multiplet spectrum to recover connectivity through the $n+1$ rule.\n"
msgstr "**NMR spectroscopy (chemical shift at $J$-coupling)** — pag-simulate ng maliit na molekula sa ilang qubit at pagbasa sa multiplet spectrum nito para makuha ang koneksyon sa pamamagitan ng $n+1$ rule.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each concept we first give the minimal theory, then implement the experiment in Qiskit following the four-step *Qiskit patterns* workflow.\n"
msgstr "Para sa bawat konsepto, ibibigay muna namin ang minimal na teorya, saka ipapatupad ang experiment sa Qiskit ayon sa apat na hakbang na workflow ng *Qiskit patterns*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theory {#theory}"
msgstr "Teorya {#theory}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spin-1/2 particles in a magnetic field {#spin-12-particles-in-a-magnetic-field}"
msgstr "Mga spin-1/2 na particle sa magnetic field {#spin-12-particles-in-a-magnetic-field}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A spin-1/2 nucleus has a magnetic moment $\\boldsymbol{\\mu} = \\gamma \\hbar \\mathbf{I}$, where $\\gamma$ is the gyromagnetic ratio. In a static field $B_0$ along $z$, the two spin states split in energy (the **Zeeman effect**):\n"
msgstr "Ang spin-1/2 na nucleus ay may magnetic moment na $\\boldsymbol{\\mu} = \\gamma \\hbar \\mathbf{I}$, kung saan ang $\\gamma$ ay ang gyromagnetic ratio. Sa static na field na $B_0$ sa direksyong $z$, nahahati sa enerhiya ang dalawang spin state (ang **Zeeman effect**):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$E_{\\pm} = \\mp \\tfrac{1}{2}\\gamma \\hbar B_0, \\qquad \\Delta E = \\gamma \\hbar B_0 = \\hbar \\omega_0 .$$\n"
msgstr "$$E_{\\pm} = \\mp \\tfrac{1}{2}\\gamma \\hbar B_0, \\qquad \\Delta E = \\gamma \\hbar B_0 = \\hbar \\omega_0 .$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The energy gap defines the **Larmor (resonance) frequency** $\\omega_0 = \\gamma B_0$. The magnetic moment **precesses** about $B_0$ at this same frequency.\n"
msgstr "Binibigyang-kahulugan ng energy gap ang **Larmor (resonance) frequency** na $\\omega_0 = \\gamma B_0$. Ang magnetic moment ay **nagpe-precess** sa paligid ng $B_0$ sa parehong frequency na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To rotate the spin we apply an oscillating RF field at (or near) $\\omega_0$. In the frame rotating at the drive frequency (the **rotating frame**), a resonant drive rotates the Bloch vector about an axis in the $x$-$y$ plane. How far it rotates (the **flip angle**) is set by the pulse's strength and duration. Two choices matter most: a $90^\\circ$ pulse tips a $+1/2$ spin into the transverse plane, and a $180^\\circ$ pulse rotates it fully to $-1/2$.\n"
msgstr "Para i-rotate ang spin, naglalapat tayo ng oscillating na RF field sa (o malapit sa) $\\omega_0$. Sa frame na umiikot sa drive frequency (ang **rotating frame**), ang resonant na drive ay nagro-rotate sa Bloch vector sa paligid ng axis sa $x$-$y$ plane. Ang lakas at tagal ng pulse ang nagtatakda kung gaano kalayo ang rotation (ang **flip angle**). Dalawang pagpipilian ang pinakamahalaga: itinutumba ng $90^\\circ$ na pulse ang $+1/2$ na spin papunta sa transverse plane, at ganap itong ini-rotate ng $180^\\circ$ na pulse papunta sa $-1/2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Translating between NMR and quantum computing jargon {#translating-between-nmr-and-quantum-computing-jargon}"
msgstr "Pagsasalin sa pagitan ng jargon ng NMR at quantum computing {#translating-between-nmr-and-quantum-computing-jargon}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit is a two-level system, mathematically identical to a spin-1/2 in a magnetic field &mdash; so while we're running on a quantum processor rather than a nucleus, the physics is the same physics that underlies NMR. Only the vocabulary differs. This table helps you talk to physical chemists and quantum-computing specialists alike.\n"
msgstr "Ang qubit ay isang two-level system, na matematikal na kapareho ng spin-1/2 sa magnetic field &mdash; kaya kahit sa quantum processor tayo tumatakbo at hindi sa nucleus, ang pisika ay ang parehong pisika na pinagbabatayan ng NMR. Bokabularyo lang ang magkaiba. Makakatulong ang talahanayang ito para makipag-usap ka sa mga physical chemist at quantum-computing specialist.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| NMR / spin-1/2 | Quantum processor (qubit) |\n"
"| ---|---|\n"
"| Spin-up / spin-down | $\\ket{0}$ / $\\ket{1}$ |\n"
"| Zeeman gap $\\Delta E = \\hbar\\omega_0$ | Qubit transition energy $\\hbar\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Larmor frequency $\\omega_0$ | Qubit frequency $\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Resonant RF pulse (flip angle $\\theta$) | Single-qubit rotation gate $R_X(\\theta)$ |\n"
"| $90^\\circ$ / $180^\\circ$ pulse | $R_X(\\pi/2)$ / $R_X(\\pi)$ |\n"
"| Spin-lattice relaxation $T_1$ | Qubit energy-relaxation time $T_1$ |\n"
"| Spin-spin relaxation $T_2$ | Qubit dephasing time $T_2$ |\n"
"| Nutation | Rabi oscillations |\n"
"| Free induction decay (FID), Hahn echo | Ramsey, echo sequences |\n"
msgstr ""
"| NMR / spin-1/2 | Quantum processor (qubit) |\n"
"| ---|---|\n"
"| Spin-up / spin-down | $\\ket{0}$ / $\\ket{1}$ |\n"
"| Zeeman gap $\\Delta E = \\hbar\\omega_0$ | Enerhiya ng transition ng qubit $\\hbar\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Larmor frequency $\\omega_0$ | Frequency ng qubit $\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Resonant na RF pulse (flip angle $\\theta$) | Single-qubit rotation gate $R_X(\\theta)$ |\n"
"| $90^\\circ$ / $180^\\circ$ na pulse | $R_X(\\pi/2)$ / $R_X(\\pi)$ |\n"
"| Spin-lattice relaxation $T_1$ | Oras ng energy-relaxation ng qubit na $T_1$ |\n"
"| Spin-spin relaxation $T_2$ | Oras ng dephasing ng qubit na $T_2$ |\n"
"| Nutation | Mga Rabi oscillation |\n"
"| Free induction decay (FID), Hahn echo | Mga Ramsey at echo sequence |\n"

