# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Experiment: Rabi oscillations (nutation) {#experiment-rabi-oscillations-nutation}"
msgstr "Experiment: Mga Rabi oscillation (nutation) {#experiment-rabi-oscillations-nutation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theory {#theory-1}"
msgstr "Teorya {#theory-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drive a spin on resonance and its Bloch vector rotates steadily from pole to pole &mdash; it **nutates**. If we apply a rotation of flip angle $\\theta$ about the $x$-axis to a qubit starting in $|0\\rangle$, the probability of finding it in $|1\\rangle$ is:\n"
msgstr "Kapag pinagana mo ang spin nang on resonance, tuluy-tuloy na umiikot ang Bloch vector nito mula pole hanggang pole &mdash; ito ay **nagnu-nutate**. Kung maglalapat tayo ng rotation na may flip angle na $\\theta$ sa paligid ng $x$-axis sa isang qubit na nagsisimula sa $|0\\rangle$, ang probability na mahanap ito sa $|1\\rangle$ ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$P_1(\\theta) = \\sin^2\\!\\left(\\tfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\bigl(1 - \\cos\\theta\\bigr).$$\n"
msgstr "$$P_1(\\theta) = \\sin^2\\!\\left(\\tfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\bigl(1 - \\cos\\theta\\bigr).$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the **Rabi curve**. Its first maximum is the $\\pi$ pulse (full inversion, the $180^\\circ$ pulse); a $\\pi/2$ pulse is a quarter-turn (the $90^\\circ$ pulse that tips a spin into the transverse plane). In NMR this curve is how you *calibrate* your pulses.\n"
msgstr "Ito ang **Rabi curve**. Ang unang maximum nito ay ang $\\pi$ na pulse (ganap na inversion, ang $180^\\circ$ na pulse); ang $\\pi/2$ na pulse ay isang kapat na ikot (ang $90^\\circ$ na pulse na nagtutumba ng spin papunta sa transverse plane). Sa NMR, ganito mo *ka-calibrate* ang iyong mga pulse.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Experimental caveat\">\n"
"A *literal* Rabi experiment sweeps the drive amplitude or duration in time. That requires pulse-level control, which was removed in Qiskit v2.0. Here we instead sweep the **rotation angle** $\\theta$ of an $R_X(\\theta)$ gate. The curve and the $\\pi$/$\\pi/2$ identification are identical; the only difference is that we choose an angle directly instead of calibrating a pulse length. On hardware with *fractional gates*, $R_X(\\theta)$ for arbitrary $\\theta$ runs natively.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Experimental caveat\">\n"
"Ang *literal* na Rabi experiment ay nag-i-sweep ng drive amplitude o duration sa oras. Nangangailangan iyon ng pulse-level na kontrol, na inalis sa Qiskit v2.0. Dito, ini-sweep natin sa halip ang **rotation angle** na $\\theta$ ng isang $R_X(\\theta)$ na gate. Pareho ang curve at ang pagkilala sa $\\pi$/$\\pi/2$; ang pagkakaiba lang ay direkta tayong pumipili ng anggulo sa halip na mag-calibrate ng haba ng pulse. Sa hardware na may *fractional gates*, native na tumatakbo ang $R_X(\\theta)$ para sa anumang $\\theta$.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Bloch-sphere view {#a-bloch-sphere-view}"
