# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Left alone, an excited spin gives up energy to its surroundings (the \"lattice\") and relaxes back toward thermal equilibrium. The excited-state population decays exponentially with the **spin-lattice relaxation time** $T_1$:\n"
msgstr "Kapag pinabayaan, ang isang excited na spin ay nagbibigay ng enerhiya sa paligid nito (ang \"lattice\") at bumabalik sa thermal equilibrium. Ang populasyon ng excited state ay nabubulok nang exponential ayon sa **spin-lattice relaxation time** na $T_1$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$P_1(\\tau) = e^{-\\tau/T_1}.$$\n"
msgstr "$$P_1(\\tau) = e^{-\\tau/T_1}.$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a chemist, $T_1$ sets the **recycle delay** you must wait between scans for quantitative NMR, and it reports on **molecular tumbling** and dynamics. On a qubit it is the energy-relaxation time, and is one of the two main numbers used to model the decoherence effects in a quantum computer.\n"
msgstr "Para sa isang chemist, itinatakda ng $T_1$ ang **recycle delay** na kailangan mong hintayin sa pagitan ng mga scan para sa quantitative NMR, at nagbibigay ito ng impormasyon tungkol sa **molecular tumbling** at dynamics. Sa isang qubit, ito ang energy-relaxation time, at isa ito sa dalawang pangunahing numerong ginagamit para imodelo ang mga epekto ng decoherence sa isang quantum computer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The experiment.** Prepare $|1\\rangle$ with an $X$ gate (a $\\pi$ pulse), wait a variable delay $\\tau$, then measure. The fraction still in $|1\\rangle$ traces out the decay.\n"
msgstr "**Ang eksperimento.** Ihanda ang $|1\\rangle$ gamit ang $X$ gate (isang $\\pi$ pulse), maghintay ng variable na delay na $\\tau$, saka sukatin. Ang bahaging nasa $|1\\rangle$ pa rin ang bumubuo ng decay.\n"

