#, no-wrap
msgid "Below, we simulate an AX$_2$ system with three qubits.\n"
msgstr "Sa ibaba, sini-simulate natin ang isang AX$_2$ system gamit ang tatlong qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-3}"
msgstr "Suriin ang pag-unawa mo {#check-your-understanding-3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read each question, think about your answer, then click the triangle to reveal the solution.\n"
msgstr "Basahin ang bawat tanong, pag-isipan ang sagot mo, saka i-click ang tatsulok para ipakita ang solusyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the AX spectrum the two doublets are separated (center-to-center) by 12 Hz, and the two lines within each doublet are 2 Hz apart. Which number is the chemical-shift difference and which is the coupling constant $J$? If you moved to a spectrometer with twice the magnetic field, which one would change?\n"
msgstr "Sa AX spectrum, ang dalawang doublet ay pinaghihiwalay (center-to-center) ng 12 Hz, at ang dalawang linya sa loob ng bawat doublet ay 2 Hz ang layo. Alin ang pagkakaiba ng chemical shift at alin ang coupling constant na $J$? Kung lilipat ka sa spectrometer na may doble ang magnetic field, alin ang magbabago?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The 12 Hz center-to-center separation is the **chemical-shift difference** ($\\nu_1-\\nu_2$); the 2 Hz line spacing is the **coupling constant $J$**. Chemical shifts come from shielding of $B_0$, so they scale with the field. At twice the field the separation doubles to 24 Hz. The coupling $J$ is a through-bond molecular property and is field-independent, so it stays 2 Hz. Chemists tell shift from coupling by watching how a splitting scales with field.\n"
msgstr "Ang 12 Hz na center-to-center na paghihiwalay ay ang **pagkakaiba ng chemical shift** ($\\nu_1-\\nu_2$); ang 2 Hz na pagitan ng linya ay ang **coupling constant na $J$**. Nagmumula ang mga chemical shift sa shielding ng $B_0$, kaya sumasabay sila sa field. Sa doble ng field, dumodoble ang paghihiwalay sa 24 Hz. Ang coupling na $J$ ay through-bond na katangian ng molecule at hindi nakadepende sa field, kaya nananatili itong 2 Hz. Natutukoy ng mga chemist ang shift mula sa coupling sa pagmamasid kung paano sumasabay ang isang paghahati sa field.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using the $n+1$ rule, predict the A multiplet if a *third* equivalent X spin were added (an AX$_3$ system), and explain why the two equivalent X spins in AX$_2$ produce no splitting of each other.\n"
msgstr "Gamit ang $n+1$ rule, hulaan ang A multiplet kung magdadagdag ng *pangatlong* equivalent na X spin (isang AX$_3$ system), at ipaliwanag kung bakit hindi naghahati sa isa't isa ang dalawang equivalent na X spin sa AX$_2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
"With $n=3$ equivalent neighbors, A becomes a 1:3:3:1 quartet. Equivalent spins don't split each other because their coupling shifts the relevant energy levels all by the same amount, so the gaps between those levels &mdash; the frequencies we see &mdash; don't change.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Sagot\">\n"
"Sa $n=3$ na equivalent na kapitbahay, nagiging 1:3:3:1 na quartet ang A. Hindi naghahati sa isa't isa ang mga equivalent na spin dahil inililipat ng coupling nila ang mga kaugnay na energy level nang pare-pareho ang halaga, kaya ang mga agwat sa pagitan ng mga level na iyon &mdash; ang mga frequency na nakikita natin &mdash; ay hindi nagbabago.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conclusion {#conclusion}"
msgstr "Konklusyon {#conclusion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We have used a real quantum computer to explore how nuclear spins precess and decohere in an NMR experiment, and how to interpret the resulting spectra. It's worth stepping back to review why this was possible at all, and why it's more than a curiosity.\n"
msgstr "Gumamit tayo ng tunay na quantum computer para tuklasin kung paano nagpe-precess at nagde-decohere ang mga nuclear spin sa isang NMR experiment, at kung paano bigyang-kahulugan ang mga nagreresultang spectra. Sulit na umatras sandali at repasuhin kung bakit ito naging posible, at kung bakit higit pa ito sa isang kuryosidad lang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit and a spin-1/2 nucleus are, mathematically, the same object: two-level quantum systems living on the Bloch sphere, rotated by resonant pulses, precessing about an axis, and losing coherence to their surroundings. The entire vocabulary of this module (the Larmor frequency, the rotating frame, $T_1$, $T_2$, and $T_2^*$, Ramsey fringes, the Hahn echo) belongs to NMR and quantum computing equally. What a chemist calls a *chemical shift*, a quantum engineer calls a *single-qubit $Z$ rotation*; what a chemist calls a *$J$-coupling*, a quantum engineer calls a *$ZZ$ interaction*. The two fields have been describing the same physics in different words.\n"
msgstr "Ang qubit at ang spin-1/2 na nucleus ay, sa matematika, iisang bagay: mga two-level na quantum system sa Bloch sphere, na pinaiikot ng mga resonant na pulse, nagpe-precess sa isang axis, at nawawalan ng coherence sa kanilang paligid. Ang buong bokabularyo ng module na ito (ang Larmor frequency, ang rotating frame, $T_1$, $T_2$, at $T_2^*$, Ramsey fringes, ang Hahn echo) ay pag-aari ng NMR at quantum computing nang pantay. Ang tawag ng chemist na *chemical shift* ay tinatawag ng quantum engineer na *single-qubit $Z$ rotation*; ang tawag ng chemist na *$J$-coupling* ay tinatawag ng quantum engineer na *$ZZ$ interaction*. Iisang pisika ang inilalarawan ng dalawang larangan sa magkaibang salita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That connection is historical, not just conceptual: NMR was one of the first platforms to run real quantum algorithms. By 2001, a molecule in solution had executed Shor's algorithm to factor 15, with each nuclear spin serving as a qubit. NMR also handed quantum computing much of its control toolkit. The spin echo, CPMG pulse trains, composite pulses, and dynamical decoupling were all invented by spectroscopists decades before qubits needed them to fight decoherence. There is a satisfying symmetry in what we just did: the field that gave birth to early quantum computers is now something a quantum computer can simulate.\n"
msgstr "Makasaysayan ang koneksyong iyon, hindi lang konseptwal: ang NMR ay isa sa mga unang platform na nagpatakbo ng tunay na quantum algorithm. Noong 2001, isang molecule sa solusyon ang nagpatakbo ng algorithm ni Shor para i-factor ang 15, kung saan ang bawat nuclear spin ay nagsilbing qubit. Ibinigay din ng NMR sa quantum computing ang malaking bahagi ng toolkit nito sa kontrol. Ang spin echo, mga CPMG pulse train, composite pulse, at dynamical decoupling ay pawang naimbento ng mga spectroscopist mga dekada bago pa kailanganin ng mga qubit ang mga ito para labanan ang decoherence. May kasiya-siyang simetriya sa ginawa natin: ang larangang nagsilang sa mga unang quantum computer ay isa na ngayong bagay na kayang i-simulate ng quantum computer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Review and questions {#review-and-questions}"
msgstr "Pagsusuri at mga tanong {#review-and-questions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Mga kritikal na konsepto {#critical-concepts}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit is an engineered two-level system equivalent to a spin-1/2; its $|0\\rangle/|1\\rangle$, frequency, gates, $T_1$, and $T_2$ are the direct analogs of NMR quantities.\n"
msgstr "Ang qubit ay isang engineered na two-level system na katumbas ng spin-1/2; ang $|0\\rangle/|1\\rangle$, frequency, mga gate, $T_1$, at $T_2$ nito ay direktang katumbas ng mga dami sa NMR.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A resonant pulse rotates the Bloch vector; the flip angle sets the rotation, and the Rabi/nutation curve $P_1=\\sin^2(\\theta/2)$ identifies $\\pi$ and $\\pi/2$ rotations.\n"
msgstr "Pinaiikot ng isang resonant na pulse ang Bloch vector; itinatakda ng flip angle ang rotation, at ang Rabi/nutation curve na $P_1=\\sin^2(\\theta/2)$ ang nagtutukoy sa mga $\\pi$ at $\\pi/2$ na rotation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$T_1$ is energy (spin-lattice) relaxation; $T_2$ is phase (spin-spin) relaxation; $T_2^{*}$ additionally includes reversible static dephasing that a Hahn echo refocuses.\n"
msgstr "Ang $T_1$ ay energy (spin-lattice) relaxation; ang $T_2$ ay phase (spin-spin) relaxation; ang $T_2^{*}$ ay may kasama pang reversible na static dephasing na nire-refocus ng Hahn echo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A molecule is a set of coupled spins: chemical shift sets each peak's position, and $J$-coupling splits peaks into multiplets following the $n+1$ rule, which together encode chemical environment and connectivity.\n"
msgstr "Ang molecule ay isang hanay ng magkakakabit na spin: itinatakda ng chemical shift ang posisyon ng bawat peak, at hinahati ng $J$-coupling ang mga peak tungo sa mga multiplet ayon sa $n+1$ rule, na magkasamang nag-eencode ng chemical environment at connectivity.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "True / false {#true-false}"
msgstr "Totoo / Mali {#true-false}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The Larmor frequency is the energy gap between the two spin states divided by $\\hbar$.\n"
msgstr "T/F Ang Larmor frequency ay ang energy gap sa pagitan ng dalawang spin state na hinati sa $\\hbar$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F A $90^\\circ$ ($\\pi/2$) pulse fully inverts an equilibrium spin.\n"
msgstr "T/F Ang $90^\\circ$ ($\\pi/2$) na pulse ay lubusang bumabaligtad sa isang spin na nasa equilibrium.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F $T_2^{*}$ is generally longer than $T_2$.\n"
msgstr "T/F Ang $T_2^{*}$ ay karaniwang mas mahaba kaysa sa $T_2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The Hahn echo refocuses irreversible spin-spin dephasing.\n"
msgstr "T/F Nire-refocus ng Hahn echo ang irreversible na spin-spin dephasing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F In an AX$_2$ system the A nucleus appears as a 1:2:1 triplet.\n"
msgstr "T/F Sa isang AX$_2$ system, lumilitaw ang A nucleus bilang 1:2:1 triplet.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The coupling constant $J$ doubles when you double the spectrometer's magnetic field.\n"
msgstr "T/F Dumodoble ang coupling constant na $J$ kapag dinoble mo ang magnetic field ng spectrometer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F Removing Qiskit Pulse makes it impossible to measure $T_1$ on current hardware.\n"
msgstr "T/F Ang pag-alis ng Qiskit Pulse ay nagiging imposible ang pagsukat ng $T_1$ sa kasalukuyang hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Short answer {#short-answer}"
msgstr "Maikling sagot {#short-answer}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Explain in two sentences why a single $\\pi$ pulse is a poor way to detect a $5\\%$ flip-angle error, and how chaining pulses fixes this.\n"
msgstr "Ipaliwanag sa dalawang pangungusap kung bakit mahinang paraan ang isang $\\pi$ pulse para matukoy ang $5\\%$ na flip-angle error, at kung paano ito naaayos ng pagkakadena ng mga pulse.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A sample shows broad NMR lines. In terms of $T_2$, what does that tell you, and what qubit quantity is the analog?\n"
msgstr "Ang isang sample ay nagpapakita ng malalapad na NMR line. Sa usapin ng $T_2$, ano ang ipinapahiwatig nito, at ano ang katumbas na dami sa qubit?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Give the qubit analog of each: (a) the recycle delay, (b) the $90^\\circ$ pulse, (c) the chemical shift.\n"
msgstr "Ibigay ang katumbas sa qubit ng bawat isa: (a) ang recycle delay, (b) ang $90^\\circ$ na pulse, (c) ang chemical shift.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using the $n+1$ rule, explain why an ethyl group (CH$_3$CH$_2$–) shows a 1:2:1 triplet and a 1:3:3:1 quartet, and identify which group produces which multiplet.\n"
msgstr "Gamit ang $n+1$ rule, ipaliwanag kung bakit ang isang ethyl group (CH$_3$CH$_2$–) ay nagpapakita ng 1:2:1 triplet at 1:3:3:1 quartet, at tukuyin kung aling grupo ang gumagawa ng aling multiplet.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Challenge problems {#challenge-problems}"
msgstr "Mga challenge problem {#challenge-problems}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Carr-Purcell train.** Modify the Hahn echo to insert $n$ equally spaced $\\pi$ pulses (a CPMG-style train) and measure $T_2$ as a function of $n$. Discuss why more refocusing pulses can lengthen the apparent $T_2$.\n"
msgstr "**Carr-Purcell train.** Baguhin ang Hahn echo para maglagay ng $n$ na pantay ang pagitan na $\\pi$ pulse (isang CPMG-style na train) at sukatin ang $T_2$ bilang function ng $n$. Talakayin kung bakit maaaring pahabain ng mas maraming refocusing pulse ang apparent na $T_2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pulse-error amplification.** Build a circuit that applies $R_X(\\pi)$ $\\,n$ times to $|0\\rangle$ and plot $P_1$ vs $n$ for a deliberately mis-set angle $R_X(1.05\\pi)$. Show how the error becomes visible as $n$ grows. **Hint:** put a barrier after every rotation; otherwise the transpiler may combine the repeated rotations into a single equivalent gate.\n"
msgstr "**Pagpapalaki ng error ng pulse.** Bumuo ng circuit na naglalapat ng $R_X(\\pi)$ nang $\\,n$ beses sa $|0\\rangle$ at i-plot ang $P_1$ laban sa $n$ para sa sadyang maling anggulong $R_X(1.05\\pi)$. Ipakita kung paano nagiging nakikita ang error habang lumalaki ang $n$. **Hint:** maglagay ng barrier pagkatapos ng bawat rotation; kung hindi, maaaring pagsamahin ng transpiler ang mga paulit-ulit na rotation tungo sa iisang katumbas na gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ethyl group.** Using `fid_circuit`, build the proton spectrum of an ethyl fragment (CH$_3$–CH$_2$): five qubits, with the three CH$_3$ protons sharing one chemical shift and the two CH$_2$ protons another, and every CH$_3$–CH$_2$ pair coupled by the same $J$ (no coupling within an equivalent group). Predict the pattern with the $n+1$ rule, then simulate it; you should recover a 1:3:3:1 quartet (CH$_2$) and a 1:2:1 triplet (CH$_3$).\n"
msgstr "**Ethyl group.** Gamit ang `fid_circuit`, buuin ang proton spectrum ng isang ethyl fragment (CH$_3$–CH$_2$): limang qubit, kung saan ang tatlong CH$_3$ proton ay may iisang chemical shift at ang dalawang CH$_2$ proton ay may isa pa, at ang bawat CH$_3$–CH$_2$ pair ay magkakabit sa parehong $J$ (walang coupling sa loob ng equivalent na grupo). Hulaan ang pattern gamit ang $n+1$ rule, saka i-simulate; dapat makuha mo ang 1:3:3:1 quartet (CH$_2$) at 1:2:1 triplet (CH$_3$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix (optional): Trotterized evolution — let decoherence set the linewidth {#appendix-optional-trotterized-evolution-let-decoherence-set-the-linewidth}"
msgstr "Appendix (opsyonal): Trotterized na ebolusyon — hayaang decoherence ang magtakda ng linewidth {#appendix-optional-trotterized-evolution-let-decoherence-set-the-linewidth}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the [NMR spectroscopy of a molecule](#nmr-spectroscopy) section, the evolution $e^{-iHt}$ is applied in a single layer whose depth does **not** grow with $t$, so the FID does not decay on its own and we impose the linewidth with the $e^{-t/T_2}$ apodization window. This optional cell takes the opposite approach. It breaks the evolution into $p$ **Trotter steps** and puts a **barrier** after each step (so the transpiler cannot merge them back into one layer). Time point $k$ uses $k$ steps, so the circuit depth grows with time.\n"
msgstr "Sa seksyong [NMR spectroscopy ng isang molecule](#nmr-spectroscopy), inilalapat ang ebolusyong $e^{-iHt}$ sa iisang layer na ang lalim ay **hindi** lumalaki kasabay ng $t$, kaya hindi nabubulok nang kusa ang FID at ipinapataw natin ang linewidth gamit ang $e^{-t/T_2}$ na apodization window. Kabaligtaran ang diskarte ng opsyonal na cell na ito. Hinahati nito ang ebolusyon sa $p$ na **Trotter step** at naglalagay ng **barrier** pagkatapos ng bawat step (para hindi maibalik ng transpiler ang mga ito sa iisang layer). Ang time point na $k$ ay gumagamit ng $k$ na step, kaya lumalaki ang lalim ng circuit kasabay ng oras.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because every term in $H$ commutes, this is *exact*: on a noiseless simulator it gives the same sharp peaks. But on a **noise-model backend or real hardware** the accumulating gate error makes the FID decay by itself, and that decay is what sets the linewidth. This is the $T_2\\leftrightarrow$linewidth idea of the [$T_2$, $T_2^*$ experiment](#t2t2star) section, now arising from real decoherence instead of a processing window. We run both the **AX** system (two doublets) and the **AX$_2$** system (a 1:2:1 triplet plus a doublet) this way.\n"
msgstr "Dahil nagko-commute ang bawat termino sa $H$, *eksakto* ito: sa noiseless na simulator, nagbibigay ito ng parehong matatalas na peak. Pero sa **noise-model backend o tunay na hardware**, ang naiipong gate error ay nagiging dahilan para mabulok nang kusa ang FID, at iyon ang nagtatakda ng linewidth. Ito ang ideya ng $T_2\\leftrightarrow$linewidth sa seksyong [$T_2$, $T_2^*$ experiment](#t2t2star), na ngayon ay nagmumula sa tunay na decoherence sa halip na processing window. Pinapatakbo natin ang parehong **AX** system (dalawang doublet) at **AX$_2$** system (isang 1:2:1 triplet at isang doublet) sa ganitong paraan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two practical notes to consider. First, the cost is depth: the deepest AX circuit uses $\\sim\\!47$ two-qubit gates and the AX$_2$ version about twice that, so both are far noisier and more expensive than the exact version. Secondly, each spin system is still submitted as one job, and every time point reuses the same physical-qubit layout selected in the spectroscopy section. If `USE_BATCH=True`, these jobs also use the optional notebook-wide Batch.\n"
msgstr "Dalawang praktikal na paalala. Una, ang gastos ay nasa lalim: ang pinakamalalim na AX circuit ay gumagamit ng $\\sim\\!47$ two-qubit gate at halos doble niyon ang AX$_2$ na bersyon, kaya mas maingay at mas magastos ang dalawa kaysa sa eksaktong bersyon. Pangalawa, isinusumite pa rin bilang isang job ang bawat spin system, at ginagamit muli ng bawat time point ang parehong physical-qubit layout na pinili sa spectroscopy section. Kung `USE_BATCH=True`, ginagamit din ng mga job na ito ang opsyonal na notebook-wide na Batch.\n"
